                  "text": "**Analyzing Verifier Code**\n\nI'm now diving into the verifier code, focusing on how it identifies the most prevalent color within an image. So far, I've seen it extract corner cells and determine the dominant color from these corners, which provides a preliminary assessment of the overall color palette. The next step will be to see what happens when the dominant corner color is combined with all colors in the image palette.\n\n\n**Deconstructing Color Logic**\n\nI've just unraveled the `argmin` function. It seems it is being used to find a color in the palette *other* than `x3`, which is the dominant color. After that, I noticed that all other colors, except `x3`, are replaced with `x6`, which contains either the divider lines or other colors. Then, it uses frontiers to separate out full rows or full columns of uniform color.\n\n\n",
